WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.160 line:82%
Chapter 12. The speaking check. Students speak into their phones, and the laptop listens.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:18.215 line:82%
The first time, open Settings, then "Speaking check", and install it. Choose Base, or Small for better results. It is free, and it works with no internet.

00:00:18.672 --> 00:00:26.595 line:82%
Read aloud is in Activities and games, Listen and read, Dictation. Make a dictation with your sentences.

00:00:27.076 --> 00:00:30.515 line:82%
Press "Start", choose "Read aloud", and open it.

00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:36.696 line:82%
Students tap their name. Then press "Start".

00:00:38.912 --> 00:00:45.536 line:82%
Each student reads the sentences at their own speed. They can listen first, normal or slowly.

00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:50.296 line:82%
The student taps "Record", reads the sentence, and taps "Stop".

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:07.875 line:82%
The laptop writes what it heard, and checks every word. Green is clear, orange is not very clear, and red is missing. Here, "goes" was missing.

00:01:08.326 --> 00:01:12.956 line:82%
The student has three tries for each sentence. The best one counts.

00:01:13.414 --> 00:01:19.276 line:82%
Your screen shows each student's score for each sentence. Click a score to hear the recording.

00:01:19.732 --> 00:01:26.037 line:82%
These scores also go to the Skill map, as "Pronunciation", and into the parents' report.

00:01:26.491 --> 00:01:32.956 line:82%
Time to speak has a voice recorder too. Open a speaking activity of your book, and press "Start".

00:01:33.408 --> 00:01:38.796 line:82%
Each student gets a card with help for their level. The student records their talk.

00:02:09.718 --> 00:02:18.090 line:82%
Then taps "Check my speaking". The laptop shows what they said, how fast, and the key words and phrases they used. Great work!
